  circleX, circleY, circleRadius / 2,
  circleX, circleY, circleRadius
);
gradient.addColorStop(0, 'blue');
gradient.addColorStop(1, 'green');

// Draw the circle
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(circleX, circleY, circleRadius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
ctx.fillStyle = gradient;
ctx.strokeStyle = 'transparent';
ctx.lineWidth = borderWidth;
ctx.setLineDash(borderDash);
ctx.shadowBlur = shadowBlur;
ctx.shadowColor = shadowColor;
ctx.shadowOffsetX = shadowOffsetX;
ctx.shadowOffsetY = shadowOffsetY;
ctx.fill();
ctx.stroke();
```

In this code, a circular gradient is created using `createRadialGradient()`, with the center of the gradient at the center of the circle and the radius of the gradient ranging from half the circle radius to the full circle radius. Two color stops are added to the gradient, with blue at the center and green at the edge of the gradient. 

The `fill()` method is used to fill the circle with the gradient, and the `stroke()` method is used to draw the dashed border around the circle. The `strokeStyle` property is set to `'transparent'` so that the border is not visible on top of the gradient fill.

