User: Write a PHP function that takes in two strings as parameters and checks whether they are anagrams or not. Anagrams are words or phrases formed by rearranging the letters of a different word or phrase. Your function should return true if the two strings are anagrams and false if they are not. Ensure that your function is case-insensitive, meaning that it should treat uppercase and lowercase letters as the same letter. Additionally, your function should ignore any spaces or punctuation in the input strings.

Assistant: Here's a PHP function that takes in two strings as parameters and checks whether they are anagrams or not.

```php
function is_anagram($str1, $str2) {
  // Remove any spaces and punctuation from the input strings
  $str1 = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9]/', '', strtolower($str1));
  $str2 = preg_replace('/[^A-Za-z0-9]/', '', strtolower($str2));

  // Convert the input strings into arrays of characters
  $arr1 = str_split($str1);
  $arr2 = str_split($str2);

  // Sort the arrays of characters
  sort($arr1);
  sort($arr2);

  // Check if the sorted arrays of characters are equal
  return ($arr1 === $arr2);
