User: Write a program in MATLAB that simulates the behavior of a simple pendulum of length L and mass m using physics principles such as gravity and Newton's laws of motion. The program should take into account the initial angle at which the pendulum is released, as well as any damping or friction in the system. The simulation should display the pendulum's position and velocity at each time step, and generate a graph of the pendulum's motion over time. The program should also output the period and frequency of the oscillations of the pendulum. Use clear comments and variable names to ensure the code is easy to understand and modify.

Assistant: % Simple Pendulum Simulation in MATLAB
% By AI

clear all;
clc;

% Define parameters
L = 1; % Length of the pendulum (in meters)
m = 1; % Mass of the bob (in kilograms)
g = 9.81; % Acceleration due to gravity (in meters per second squared)
theta0 = pi/4; % Initial angle (in radians)
damping = 0.1; % Damping coefficient (in kilograms per second)
time = 10; % Total simulation time (in seconds)
dt = 0.01; % Time step (in seconds)

% Initialize variables
theta = theta0;
omega = 0;
t = 0;
data = [];

% Run simulation
while t < time
    alpha = -(g/L)*sin(theta) - damping*omega/m; % Angular acceleration
    omega = omega + alpha*dt; % Angular velocity
    theta = theta + omega*dt; % Angle
    t = t + dt; % Time
    data(end+1,:) = [t,theta,omega]; % Record data
end

% Calculate period and frequency
tmax = max(data(:,1));
tmin = min(data(:,1));
period = 2*(tmax-tmin);
frequency = 1/period;

% Display results
disp('Period and Frequency');
disp(['Period = ',num2str(period),' seconds']);
disp(['Frequency = ',num2str(frequency),' hertz']);

% Generate plot
figure;
subplot(2,1,1);
plot(data(:,1),data(:,2),'r');
title('Simple Pendulum Simulation');
xlabel('Time (s)');
ylabel('Angle (rad)');
subplot(2,1,2);
plot(data(:,1),data(:,3),'b');
xlabel('Time (s)');
ylabel('Angular Velocity (rad/s)');

