Assistant: I am incapable of visual interface or web development. However, I can provide you with a general guide on how to create a toggle button using css and javascript.

step 1: html markup
create an html element for the toggle button. It can be an <a>, a <button>, or a <div> element. Give it an id or a class name so that it can be targeted in css and javascript.

example:
```
<button id="toggle-button">toggle</button>
```

step 2: css styling
style the toggle button in css. You can give it a background color, border, padding, font-size, and any other styles that fit within the overall design of your website or application.

example:
```
#toggle-button {
  background-color: #005792;
  color: white;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  font-size: 16px;
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

step 3: javascript toggle
use javascript to create a toggle function that switches the state of the button when clicked. You can use an if/else statement or a boolean value to determine the current state of the button and change its styling and content accordingly.

example:
```
var togglebtn = document.getelementbyid("toggle-button");
var toggle = true;

function togglefunction() {
  if (toggle) {
    togglebtn.innerhtml = "off";
    togglebtn.style.backgroundcolor = "red";
    toggle = false;
  } else {
    togglebtn.innerhtml = "on";
    togglebtn.style.backgroundcolor = "#005792";
    toggle = true;
  }
}

togglebtn.addeventlistener("click", togglefunction);
```

step 4: responsive design
make sure the toggle button is responsive to different screen sizes and devices. You can use media queries in css to adjust its styling and layout for smaller screens or add accessibility features for users with disabilities.

example:
```
@media only screen and (max-width: 600px) {
  #toggle-button {
    font-size: 14px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
  }
}
```

by following these steps, you can create a toggle button that smoothly and responsively switches between states for a seamless user experience. Remember to test the button on different devices and browsers to ensure it works well and fits within the overall design of your website or application.

