User: Develop a PHP script that accepts an array of integers and checks whether the elements are in descending order or not. The script should return a boolean value of true if the array is in descending order, and false otherwise. The script should also handle ties, meaning that elements that have the same value can be considered as being in descending order. The script must be well commented and should follow standard coding practices.

Assistant: <?php

/**
 * checkIfDescendingOrder function checks whether the given array
 * is in descending order or not
 *
 * @param array $arr An array of integers to check for descending order
 * @return bool Returns true if the array is in descending order or false otherwise.
 */
function checkIfDescendingOrder($arr) {
    // Count the number of elements in the array
    $arr_length = count($arr);

    // Check if array has more than 1 elements
    if ($arr_length > 1) {
        // First element is the maximum value so far
        $max_value = $arr[0];
        // Iterate over the remaining elements of the array
        for ($i = 1; $i < $arr_length; $i++) {
            // Check if current value is greater than the maximum value so far
            if ($arr[$i] > $max_value) {
                // Return false as this is not a descending order array
                return false;
            }
            // Update the maximum value
            $max_value = $arr[$i];
        }
    }
    // Return true as array is in descending order
    return true;
}

// Example usage
$arr = array(9, 7, 5, 5, 3);
if (checkIfDescendingOrder($arr)) {
    echo "Array is in descending order";
} else {
    echo "Array is not in descending order";
}

?>

