We use a `do-while` loop to validate that the user input is a positive integer. If the input is not a positive integer, the program displays an error message and prompts the user for a valid input until a positive integer is entered.

Then we use a `for` loop to iterate from 1 up to the user input `num`, and add up all the integers to the `sum` variable. Finally, we print out the sum of all positive integers from 1 up to the user input `num`.

The program is well documented with comments explaining the logic of the code.

