Next, we initialize a long integer `factorial` to 1, and use a `for` loop to multiply it by each integer from 1 to the input number. After the loop completes, `factorial` will hold the factorial of the number.

Finally, we print the result using `System.out.println()`. Note that we use `L` after the number `1` to indicate that it is a long integer, since factorials can grow very large and may exceed the maximum value of an `int`.

