User: Write a PHP script that sends an email with a specific message and subject to a list of email addresses.

Assistant: Here is an example PHP script that uses the built-in mail function to send an email with a specific message and subject to a list of email addresses:

```
<?php
// Define email subject and message
$subject = "Your Subject Here";
$message = "Hello,\n\nThis is the message body of the email.";

// Define recipient email addresses
$recipients = array("email1@example.com", "email2@example.com");

// Loop through recipients and send email to each one
foreach ($recipients as $recipient) {
    // Set up email headers
    $headers = "From: Your Name <your_email@example.com>\r\n";
    $headers .= "Reply-To: your_email@example.com\r\n";
    $headers .= "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\r\n";

    // Send email
    if(mail($recipient, $subject, $message, $headers)) {
        echo "Email sent to $recipient\n";
    } else {
        echo "Email sending failed to $recipient\n";
    }
}
?>
```

In the above example, replace "Your Subject Here" with the desired subject of the email, and replace "Hello,\n\nThis is the message body of the email." with the desired message body.

Also, replace the array of email addresses in the $recipients variable with the actual email addresses to which you want to send the email.

Note that this PHP script assumes that the server you are running it on has a functioning email server configured. If you encounter any issues with the email not being sent, you may need to consult with your web host or system administrator to ensure that email sending is properly configured on the server.

User: Can you provide me an example of how to add attachments to the email using PHP?

Assistant: Yes! Here's an example of how to add attachments to the email with PHP:

```php
<?php
// Recipient email
$to = 'recipient@example.com';

// Email subject
$subject = 'Email with Attachment';

// Email message
$message = 'This email contains an attachment.';

// Mime boundary (optional)
$mime_boundary = md5(time());

// Headers
$headers = "From: sender@example.com\r\n";
$headers .= "Reply-To: sender@example.com\r\n";
$headers .= "MIME-Version: 1.0\r\n";
$headers .= "Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\"" . $mime_boundary . "\"\r\n";

// Attachment path and file name
$file_name = 'example_attachment.pdf';
$file_path = '/path/to/attachment/' . $file_name;
$file_type = 'application/pdf';  // MIME type of attachment

// Read the file into a variable
$file_content = file_get_contents($file_path);
$file_content = chunk_split(base64_encode($file_content));

// Attachment headers
$attachment = "--" . $mime_boundary . "\r\n";
$attachment .= "Content-Type: " . $file_type . "; name=\"" . $file_name . "\"\r\n";
$attachment .= "Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"" . $file_name . "\"\r\n";
$attachment .= "Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64\r\n\r\n";
$attachment .= $file_content . "\r\n";
$attachment .= "--" . $mime_boundary . "--\r\n";

// Combine message and attachment
$body = "--" . $mime_boundary . "\r\n";
$body .= "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\r\n";
$body .= "Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\r\n\r\n";
$body .= $message . "\r\n";
$body .= $attachment;

// Send email
if (mail($to, $subject, $body, $headers)) {
    echo "Email sent successfully.";
} else {
    echo "Email not sent.";
}
?>
```

In this example, the file is read into a variable, base64 encoded, and then attached to the email using appropriate headers. The attachment is then combined with the message into a single email body.

Make sure to customize variables like `$to`, `$subject`, `$file_name`, and `$file_path` to your specific use case.

