User: Using CSS, create a smooth and gradual folding animation for a web page's content when a button is clicked. The folding effect should be visually appealing and complement the website's overall style. The animation should not affect the website's functionality or user experience. Provide a clear and concise instruction for users to initiate the folding animation.

Assistant: To create a smooth and gradual folding animation for your web page, follow these steps:

1. First, create a container element around the content you want to fold.
2. Set its position property to "relative" and its overflow property to "hidden".
3. Add a class to this container element, e.g., "fold-container".
4. Create a button element for users to initiate the folding animation.
5. Add an event listener to this button that triggers a JavaScript function to add or remove a class from the container element.
6. In the CSS stylesheet, define the states of the container element with the class "fold-container" and its child elements, e.g., "folded" and "unfolded".
7. Create a transition property for the container element, with a duration of your choice, e.g. 0.5s or 1s, and an easing function that makes the animation look smooth, e.g., "cubic-bezier(0.42, 0, 0.58, 1)".
8. Define the styles for the folded and unfolded states of the container element, including the height, width, position, and transform properties that create a folding effect.

To initiate the folding animation, tell users to click the button element. When the button is clicked, the JavaScript function should toggle the "folded" class on the "fold-container" element. This will trigger the transition to the folded or unfolded state, depending on its current state. For example,

```
<button onclick="toggleFold()">Fold Content</button>

<div class="fold-container">
  <div class="folded">
    <!-- folded content here -->
  </div>
  <div class="unfolded">
    <!-- unfolded content here -->
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  function toggleFold() {
    var container = document.querySelector(".fold-container");
    container.classList.toggle("folded");
  }
</script>

/* CSS */
.fold-container {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: height 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.42, 0, 0.58, 1);
}

.fold-container .folded {
  height: 0;
  width: 100%;
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  transform-origin: top center;
  transform: rotateX(-90deg);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: transform 0.5s, opacity 0.5s;
}

.fold-container .unfolded {
  width: 100%;
  opacity: 1;
  transform: rotateX(0deg);
  transition: transform 0.5s, opacity 0.5s 0.3s;
}
```

