Yes, here is a step-by-step guide on how to add file transfer functionality to your chat application using Socket.io technology.

1. Install necessary packages

You will need to install the `multer` package to enable file uploads.

```
npm install multer
```

2. Create a file upload directory

You will have to create a directory to store the uploaded files. This can be done using the `fs` module.

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const uploadDir = __dirname + '/uploads';
if (!fs.existsSync(uploadDir)) {
  fs.mkdirSync(uploadDir);
}
```

3. Handle file uploads

You can handle file uploads using the `multer` middleware. You will have to add the `multer` package and configure it.

```javascript
const multer = require('multer');
const upload = multer({ dest: uploadDir });
```

Then you can define a route to handle file uploads.

```javascript
app.post('/upload', upload.single('file'), (req, res) => {
  if (!req.file) {
    return res.status(400).send('No files were uploaded');
  }

  res.status(200).send(req.file.filename);
});
```

4. Send the file to the server

You can send files to the server using the `FormData()` object in JavaScript.

```javascript
const fileInput = document.querySelector('input[type="file"]');
const file = fileInput.files[0];
const formData = new FormData();
formData.append('file', file);
fetch('/upload', { method: 'POST', body: formData });
```

5. Add the file transfer feature to the chat

To send a file to a client, you can emit an event to the server with the file information. The server can then emit the event to that specific client.

```javascript
// Server side
socket.on('send-file', ({ filename, recipient }) => {
  const filePath = `${uploadDir}/${filename}`;
  io.to(recipient).emit('file-received', { filename, filePath });
});

// Client-Side
submitBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  const recipient = selectRecipient.value;
  const filename = fileInput.files[0].name;

  // Emit an event to the server with the file information
  socket.emit('send-file', { filename, recipient });
});
```

You will then have to add an event listener for when the client receives the file. The event listener will download the file.

```javascript
// Client-Side
socket.on('file-received', ({ filename, filePath }) => {
  const link = document.createElement('a');
  link.href = `${filePath}`;
  link.download = `${filename}`;
  link.click();
});
```

In conclusion, follow the above steps to add file transfer functionality to your chat application using Socket.io. This ensures the smooth transfer of files between users in real-time.

